---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";

import bskyLogo from "@/assets/bsky_logo.svg";
---

<Layout title="About" description="About azyrite's rail blog">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>
      Welcome to my little corner of the internet where I occasionally put up
      railway-related photos and posts, mostly from my home state of NSW.
    </p>
    <p>
      I&apos;ve had an interest in trains for some time, although I only started
      properly photographing them in early 2025, when a friend kindly lent me
      their camera and I discovered the joys of photography.
    </p>
    <h2>Technical details</h2>
    <p>
      This is a simple, (mostly) statically generated site powered by <a
        href="https://astro.build"
        target="_blank">{Astro.generator}</a
      >. The code is open source for those who want to take a gander: <a
        href="https://github.com/azyritedev/railblog"
        target="_blank">GitHub</a
      >.
    </p>
    <p>
      <p>
        TailwindCSS is used for styling because I can't actually write CSS
        anymore.
      </p>
      <h2>A note on photos</h2>
      <p>
        Images have been rendered in JPEG format (from RAW camera files), and
        may have been compressed. Images may also be presented in WEBP but a
        JPEG photo should always be accessible.
      </p>
      <p>
        Some care has been taken to preserve any EXIF data attached to the
        images particularly of those images captured on a phone (which usually
        contains useful geolocation data). However, this is not guaranteed,
        especially with edited photos.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you are after the RAW photos, I might have them lying around
        somewhere. Send me an email and I'll try my best to get back to you.
      </p>
      <h1>Attributions</h1>
      <p>
        Much of the inspiration for this website including its general layout,
        theming and style was taken from <a
          href="https://railgallery.wongm.com/"
          target="_blank">Wongm's Rail Gallery</a
        >. Go check out his site, there's a lot more there!
      </p>
      <p>
        All photographs and posts are my own unless otherwise indicated. If you
        would like to use these photos for your own purposes <b
          >please send me an email beforehand.</b
        > I'd love to see what you do with them!
      </p>
      <h1>Contact</h1>
      <p>You can find me on social media:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <a
            href="https://bsky.app/profile/azyrite.bsky.social"
            class="inline-flex gap-2 items-center text-[#1185fe] not-prose"
          >
            <Image
              src={bskyLogo}
              alt="Bluesky logo"
              class="w-5"
              loading="eager"
            />
            <span class="block">azyrite.bsky.social</span>
          </a>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Or email me: <a href="mailto:azyrite-railblog@astrial.org"
          >azyrite-railblog@astrial.org</a
        >
      </p>
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
